Added optional copying of a provider's avatar into Plone's portrait storage, **off by default**. When switched on, a changed `picture_url` claim is fetched over HTTPS during claims sync and stored as the user's portrait, scaled through Plone's own helper so it is the same shape as one uploaded through user preferences. It is off by default because of what the fetch is: `picture_url` is a claim, and at plenty of providers a claim is whatever the user typed, so turning it into a server-side fetch makes the login path a request forger — a user pointing it at an address only the backend can reach gets the backend to fetch it and reads the result off their own portrait. When enabled, the fetch is HTTPS-only, short-timeout, capped by counting bytes off the stream rather than trusting a header, and refused unless the server claims an image content type; a URL is fetched only when it changes, and a URL that failed is not retried on every subsequent login. No failure here can break a login. @ericof
